For your Dijkstra code:

Time Complexity: O((V + E) log V)

Why?

Building the adjacency list:
We go through every edge once.
Time = O(E)
Priority queue:
Every time we find a shorter distance, we push into the min-heap.
A heap operation (push/pop) takes O(log V) approximately.
We can have up to O(E) such operations.
Time = O(E log V)
Processing vertices:
Each vertex is processed through the heap.
This contributes O(V log V).

So:

O(E) + O(E log V) + O(V log V)

= O((V + E) log V)

For most graphs, this is commonly written as:

O(E log V)

Space Complexity: O(V + E)

Why?

Adjacency list:
Stores V vertices and E edges.
O(V + E)
Distance array:
Stores distance for every vertex.
O(V)
Priority queue:
Can contain multiple entries for vertices.
Worst case can be O(E).

Overall:

O(V + E) + O(V) + O(E)

= O(V + E)

So the final answer is:

Time Complexity: O((V + E) log V)

Space Complexity: O(V + E)


class Solution {
  public:
    vector<int> dijkstra(int V, vector<vector<int>> &edges, int src) {
        vector<vector<pair<int,int>>>adj(V);
        vector<int>dist(V,1e9);
        vector<int>parent(V,0);
        
        for(int i = 0; i < V; i++)
        {
            parent[i] = i;
        }
        
        for(auto it : edges)
        {
            int u = it[0];
            int v = it[1];
            int wt = it[2];
            
            adj[u].push_back({v,wt});
            adj[v].push_back({u,wt});
        }
        
        //dist,node
        priority_queue<pair<int,int>,vector<pair<int,int>>,greater<pair<int,int>>>pq;
        
        dist[src] = 0;
        pq.push({0,src});
        
        while(!pq.empty())
        {
            auto [d,node] = pq.top();
            pq.pop();
            
            if(d > dist[node]) continue;
            for(auto [ngh,wt] : adj[node])
            {
                if(dist[ngh] > dist[node] + wt)
                {
                    dist[ngh] = dist[node] + wt;
                    pq.push({dist[ngh],ngh});
                }
            }
        }
        return dist;
        
        
    }
};
